      <Docs>
        <summary>Flag for use with <see cref="M:Android.Content.Intent.ParseUri(System.String,Android.Content.IntentUriType)" /> to allow parsing of unsafe information. Without this flag, <see cref="F:Android.Content.ActivityFlags.GrantReadUriPermission" />, <see cref="F:Android.Content.ActivityFlags.GrantWriteUriPermission" />, <see cref="F:Android.Content.ActivityFlags.GrantPersistableUriPermission" />, and <see cref="F:Android.Content.ActivityFlags.GrantPrefixUriPermission" /> are removed from the parsed intent. When this flag is set, those flags can be retained and can cause unexpected data access. If you do not trust the URI source, take further steps to protect yourself. In particular, when using the intent to start an activity, you should usually add <see cref="F:Android.Content.Intent.CategoryBrowsable" /> to limit the activities that can handle it.</summary>
        <remarks>
