      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>Flag for serializing and parsing an intent in the <c>android-app:</c> URI scheme. This format is useful for an HTTP or HTTPS URI delivered to a specific package:</para>
          <code>android-app://{package_id}[/{scheme}[/{host}[/{path}]]][#Intent;{...}]</code>
          <para>Only the package ID is required. A host requires a scheme, and a path requires both a scheme and a host. The <c>#Intent;</c> fragment can be used without a scheme, host, or path. This format cannot be used with a selector because the base intent has an explicit package name.</para>
          <para>Examples, each with package <c>com.example.app</c>:</para>
          <list type="bullet">
            <item><description><c>android-app://com.example.app</c>: action <c>ACTION_MAIN</c>.</description></item>
            <item><description><c>android-app://com.example.app/http/example.com/</c>: action <c>ACTION_VIEW</c>, data <c>http://example.com/</c>.</description></item>
            <item><description><c>android-app://com.example.app/http/example.com/foo?1234</c>: action <c>ACTION_VIEW</c>, data <c>http://example.com/foo?1234</c>.</description></item>
            <item><description><c>android-app://com.example.app/#Intent;action=com.example.MY_ACTION;end</c>: action <c>com.example.MY_ACTION</c>.</description></item>
            <item><description><c>android-app://com.example.app/http/example.com/foo?1234#Intent;action=com.example.MY_ACTION;end</c>: action <c>com.example.MY_ACTION</c>, data <c>http://example.com/foo?1234</c>.</description></item>
            <item><description><c>android-app://com.example.app/#Intent;action=com.example.MY_ACTION;i.some_int=100;S.some_str=hello;end</c>: action <c>com.example.MY_ACTION</c>, integer extra <c>some_int=100</c>, and string extra <c>some_str=hello</c>.</description></item>
          </list>
        </summary>
        <remarks>
          <para>Portions of this page are modifications based on work created and shared by the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/site-policies" title="Android Open Source Project">Android Open Source Project</a></format> and used according to terms described in the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5/" title="Creative Commons 2.5 Attribution License">Creative Commons 2.5 Attribution License.</a></format></para>
